WEBVTT

1
00:03:07.250 --> 00:03:08.150
Okay, me too.

2
00:03:08.150 --> 00:03:11.440
Eddie, shoot, there's no one here.

3
00:03:11.440 --> 00:04:20.790
Attorney wants a statement.

4
00:04:20.790 --> 00:04:22.110
What do you want me to say to her?

5
00:04:22.110 --> 00:05:15.740
The truth.

6
00:05:15.740 --> 00:05:18.480
It's like Snorin.

7
00:05:18.480 --> 00:05:22.050
Yeah.

8
00:05:22.050 --> 00:05:23.650
How many total?

9
00:05:23.650 --> 00:05:25.070
Got 15 in this hall here,

10
00:05:25.070 --> 00:05:27.210
about 20 in the back bedroom.

11
00:05:27.210 --> 00:05:30.290
We haven't even checked the attic under the cross base.

12
00:05:30.290 --> 00:05:35.080
Call DOJ, let them know what we have.

13
00:05:35.080 --> 00:05:37.280
Is one of the houses owned by Manuel Diaz?

14
00:05:38.400 --> 00:05:46.210
No way to connect him, but he owns it.

15
00:05:46.210 --> 00:07:48.070
Red step out.

16
00:07:48.070 --> 00:07:51.270
Such a heavy body count this close to Phoenix

17
00:07:51.290 --> 00:07:54.770
is without a doubt a major escalation for the cartels.

18
00:07:54.770 --> 00:07:56.490
There will be pressure in Washington

19
00:07:56.490 --> 00:07:58.730
to explain how such a dramatic outrage

20
00:07:58.730 --> 00:08:01.530
could happen so deep inside the American heartland.

21
00:08:02.430 --> 00:08:04.690
We may be talking about the victims of a turf war

22
00:08:04.690 --> 00:08:08.010
or maybe some illegal immigrants who are tied to a ransom,

23
00:08:08.010 --> 00:08:09.470
but it will be some weeks

24
00:08:09.470 --> 00:08:23.690
before we have a clearer picture on who the victims.

25
00:08:23.690 --> 00:08:25.610
She's been leading our kidnap response team

26
00:08:25.610 --> 00:08:26.650
for three years.

27
00:08:26.650 --> 00:08:28.450
Put her through the grinder since she got here

28
00:08:28.450 --> 00:08:30.250
and she hasn't blinked.

29
00:08:30.250 --> 00:08:31.730
She's in the front line.

30
00:08:31.750 --> 00:08:33.270
Nobody's gonna be happier than Kate

31
00:08:33.270 --> 00:08:35.070
to see these guys go down.

32
00:08:35.070 --> 00:08:36.630
So she's a thumper.

33
00:08:36.630 --> 00:08:38.830
Today was her fifth OIS.

34
00:08:38.830 --> 00:08:41.150
Five and O, not bad for a rookie.

35
00:08:41.150 --> 00:08:42.390
She's never worked cases.

36
00:08:42.390 --> 00:08:44.590
Been kicking doors since day one.

37
00:08:44.590 --> 00:08:45.410
I like her already.

38
00:08:45.410 --> 00:08:46.350
What about the partner?

39
00:08:46.350 --> 00:08:47.750
You seen the action?

40
00:08:47.750 --> 00:08:49.550
He's only been with us 18 months.

41
00:08:49.550 --> 00:08:50.990
What's his background?

42
00:08:50.990 --> 00:08:51.990
He's a sharp kid.

43
00:08:52.910 --> 00:08:55.150
ROTC's a scholar, shipped to Maryland,

44
00:08:55.150 --> 00:08:57.950
did a tour in Iraq, got his law degree from UNC.

45
00:08:59.630 --> 00:09:01.030
He's green, but he's good.

46
00:09:02.030 --> 00:09:03.550
No lawyers on this train.

47
00:09:03.550 --> 00:09:04.710
Just give me the girl.

48
00:09:06.150 --> 00:09:07.390
He did this by the book, right?

49
00:09:07.390 --> 00:09:22.050
Come on.

50
00:09:22.050 --> 00:09:35.970
Why don't you step in here, Kate?

51
00:09:35.970 --> 00:09:37.850
Quite a find today.

52
00:09:37.850 --> 00:09:39.890
The loss of two officers notwithstanding.

53
00:09:41.010 --> 00:09:42.670
Yes, sir.

54
00:09:42.670 --> 00:09:45.970
How familiar are you with Manuel Diaz's operation?

55
00:09:45.970 --> 00:09:47.810
His company, Sun Oasis,

56
00:09:47.810 --> 00:09:49.890
has 80 or so foreclosure properties.

57
00:09:49.890 --> 00:09:52.450
He has other legitimate businesses,

58
00:09:52.450 --> 00:09:53.490
but he's rumored to be linked

59
00:09:53.490 --> 00:09:55.250
with one of the Mexican cartels.

60
00:09:56.230 --> 00:09:59.270
Manuel Diaz works for the Sonora Cartel.

61
00:09:59.270 --> 00:10:01.750
He's most likely their senior member in the United States.

62
00:10:01.750 --> 00:10:05.280
What do you know about his brother?

63
00:10:05.280 --> 00:10:07.040
I wasn't aware he had one.

64
00:10:07.040 --> 00:10:08.760
Guillermo.

65
00:10:08.760 --> 00:10:09.800
His brother's name is Guillermo.

66
00:10:09.800 --> 00:10:11.400
Do you know anything about his cousin?

67
00:10:11.400 --> 00:10:12.520
I didn't know he had one of those either.

68
00:10:12.520 --> 00:10:13.560
None of that is in his file.

69
00:10:13.560 --> 00:10:18.370
His cousin is Fausto Alarcon.

70
00:10:18.370 --> 00:10:19.210
No one does.

71
00:10:19.210 --> 00:10:20.230
He's off the grid.

72
00:10:20.230 --> 00:10:22.950
He's number three in the Sonora Cartel.

73
00:10:22.950 --> 00:10:24.630
This is not my department, sir.

74
00:10:24.630 --> 00:10:27.470
Like I said, Agent Mason doesn't work narcotics.

75
00:10:27.470 --> 00:10:30.050
She runs a kidnap response team.

76
00:10:30.050 --> 00:10:30.890
Are you married?

77
00:10:32.370 --> 00:10:33.930
Am I married?

78
00:10:33.930 --> 00:10:38.000
Do you have a husband?

79
00:10:38.000 --> 00:10:41.380
Divorced?

80
00:10:41.380 --> 00:10:42.220
Kids?

81
00:10:43.700 --> 00:10:46.020
No.

82
00:10:46.020 --> 00:10:50.240
Anything else?

83
00:10:50.240 --> 00:10:59.040
Thanks, Kate, if you could wait outside, please.

84
00:10:59.040 --> 00:10:59.880
Well?

85
00:10:59.880 --> 00:11:20.670
I have no clue.

86
00:11:20.670 --> 00:11:21.510
Coming in, guys.

87
00:11:24.230 --> 00:11:29.890
Will you come back in, Kate?

88
00:11:29.890 --> 00:11:32.890
DOJ wants advisors that focus on cartels

89
00:11:32.890 --> 00:11:35.370
involved in pursuing Mr. Diaz.

90
00:11:35.430 --> 00:11:36.550
This is Matt Graver.

91
00:11:36.550 --> 00:11:38.710
He'll be leading the team.

92
00:11:38.710 --> 00:11:41.150
Isn't this Phoenix Homicide now?

93
00:11:41.150 --> 00:11:43.190
No, we're expanding the scope

94
00:11:43.190 --> 00:11:45.150
of the investigation, Matt.

95
00:11:45.150 --> 00:11:46.510
You'll act as a liaison.

96
00:11:46.510 --> 00:11:47.710
What does that mean?

97
00:11:47.710 --> 00:11:51.350
They need an agent with tactical experience like you.

98
00:11:51.350 --> 00:11:52.950
State Department is pulling an agent

99
00:11:52.950 --> 00:11:54.430
from the field that specializes

100
00:11:54.430 --> 00:11:57.370
in responding to escalated cartel activity.

101
00:11:57.370 --> 00:11:59.510
He'll be part of the team.

102
00:11:59.510 --> 00:12:02.270
You meet up with him at Luke tomorrow?

103
00:12:02.270 --> 00:12:03.710
Day after, early.

104
00:12:03.710 --> 00:12:04.750
Air Force Base?

105
00:12:04.970 --> 00:12:06.170
We're gonna go see Guillermo.

106
00:12:06.170 --> 00:12:07.610
Diaz's brother?

107
00:12:07.610 --> 00:12:10.570
That's the one.

108
00:12:10.570 --> 00:12:12.090
Where is he?

109
00:12:12.090 --> 00:12:17.950
He's in the El Paso area.

110
00:12:17.950 --> 00:12:23.120
What's our objective?

111
00:12:23.120 --> 00:12:26.960
To dramatically overreact.

112
00:12:26.960 --> 00:12:31.720
Kate, you must volunteer for an interagency task force.

113
00:12:32.840 --> 00:12:34.840
Think very hard before you respond.

114
00:12:36.280 --> 00:12:40.240
You wanna be a part of this?

115
00:12:40.240 --> 00:12:41.080
Do we get an opportunity

116
00:12:41.080 --> 00:12:47.080
of the men responsible for today?

117
00:12:47.080 --> 00:12:53.050
The men who are really responsible for today, yeah.

118
00:12:53.190 --> 00:13:09.840
I'll volunteer.

119
00:13:09.840 --> 00:13:15.790
I'll volunteer.

120
00:14:53.400 --> 00:14:54.980
Let them know that I'm not in charge of the flip-flops.

121
00:14:54.980 --> 00:14:59.250
I don't trust them.

122
00:14:59.250 --> 00:15:00.090
How you doing, son?

123
00:15:00.090 --> 00:15:09.400
Hi, Dees.

124
00:15:09.400 --> 00:15:11.320
She's on the list, but you're not.

125
00:15:11.320 --> 00:15:12.400
What was she supposed to do?

126
00:15:12.400 --> 00:15:13.240
Need you to turn this around, boy.

127
00:15:13.240 --> 00:15:14.840
That's fine, it's good.

128
00:15:14.840 --> 00:15:16.840
I'll call you when we're headed back.

129
00:15:16.840 --> 00:15:17.840
All right.

130
00:15:17.840 --> 00:15:47.650
My bird dog over there, Alejandro.

131
00:15:47.650 --> 00:15:53.000
Are you taking this?

132
00:15:53.000 --> 00:15:54.000
Yep.

133
00:15:54.000 --> 00:15:56.000
I'm doing the best for you.

134
00:15:56.000 --> 00:16:11.150
DOD flies around in private jets, huh?

135
00:16:11.150 --> 00:16:12.150
Yeah.

136
00:16:12.150 --> 00:16:13.150
You guys don't have one of these?

137
00:16:13.150 --> 00:16:14.150
Right.

138
00:16:14.150 --> 00:16:18.670
Is there any food on this flight?

139
00:16:18.670 --> 00:16:21.670
Yeah, there's some bitchin' peanuts in the back,

140
00:16:21.670 --> 00:16:24.670
but it's kind of a self-serve deal.

141
00:16:24.670 --> 00:16:37.330
Cape May, sir.

142
00:16:37.330 --> 00:16:39.330
Never been to what is before?

143
00:16:39.330 --> 00:16:42.330
Um, no, I...

144
00:16:43.330 --> 00:16:45.330
We're going to El Paso, right?

145
00:16:45.330 --> 00:16:47.330
Yeah, I...

146
00:16:47.330 --> 00:16:48.330
Okay.

147
00:16:48.330 --> 00:18:14.480
Are you okay?

148
00:18:14.480 --> 00:18:32.100
So this is your specialty.

149
00:18:32.100 --> 00:18:33.100
Hmm?

150
00:18:33.100 --> 00:18:36.100
The cartels in Mexico are your specialty.

151
00:18:36.100 --> 00:18:37.100
Yeah.

152
00:18:37.100 --> 00:18:43.120
Is there anything I should know?

153
00:18:43.120 --> 00:18:50.300
Yeah, a watch works.

154
00:18:50.300 --> 00:18:52.300
For now, let's just keep an eye on the time.

155
00:18:52.300 --> 00:19:12.820
How you been?

156
00:19:12.820 --> 00:19:13.820
Good, buddy.

157
00:19:13.820 --> 00:19:14.820
How you feeling?

158
00:19:14.820 --> 00:19:17.820
Well, when I pee, it burns.

159
00:19:17.820 --> 00:19:19.820
Maybe it's gonorrhea.

160
00:19:19.820 --> 00:19:21.820
What color is it?

161
00:19:21.820 --> 00:19:23.820
Yellow with red specks.

162
00:19:23.820 --> 00:19:25.820
Red specks are blood.

163
00:19:25.820 --> 00:19:30.900
Trying to get DOD to let me look into this conspiracy to sink Fiji.

164
00:19:30.900 --> 00:19:31.900
Fiji?

165
00:19:31.900 --> 00:19:32.900
Yeah.

166
00:19:32.900 --> 00:19:33.900
Leave Fiji alone, terrorists.

167
00:19:33.900 --> 00:19:34.900
Exactly.

168
00:19:34.900 --> 00:19:37.900
Figure a month or two over there, we'll get it all worked out.

169
00:19:37.900 --> 00:19:39.900
So who's going over there today?

170
00:19:39.900 --> 00:19:40.900
Marshals, DEA.

171
00:19:40.900 --> 00:19:41.900
I pulled a T of you, man.

172
00:19:41.900 --> 00:19:42.900
Oh, man, I love it when you say a T.

173
00:19:42.900 --> 00:19:44.900
It makes me all warm and fuzzy.

174
00:19:44.900 --> 00:19:45.900
Oh, they're a crack bunch, too.

175
00:19:45.900 --> 00:19:47.900
Just rotated back from Afghanistan.

176
00:19:47.900 --> 00:19:48.900
Wow.

177
00:19:48.900 --> 00:19:49.900
Was everybody linking up?

178
00:19:49.900 --> 00:19:51.900
AIC.

179
00:19:52.900 --> 00:20:05.750
Good, good, good.

180
00:20:05.750 --> 00:20:13.750
Mexican federal police will meet you at the border and proceed with you to the courthouse located here.

181
00:20:13.750 --> 00:20:18.500
This is a high-level target.

182
00:20:18.500 --> 00:20:26.780
The most likely spots for an attempt will be at the exchange and at the border crossing on the return.

183
00:20:26.780 --> 00:20:28.780
The marshals will enter.

184
00:20:28.780 --> 00:20:32.260
Kevin, Keith, you want to stand up?

185
00:20:32.260 --> 00:20:36.700
Now, the marshals' response team is in Laredo.

186
00:20:36.700 --> 00:20:41.700
So our friends from Delta have volunteered to come along and we'll escort the marshals on the exchange.

187
00:20:41.700 --> 00:20:44.700
And here's the man of the hour.

188
00:20:44.700 --> 00:20:45.700
Coming with or waiting here?

189
00:20:45.700 --> 00:20:47.700
We'll take the tour with you.

190
00:20:47.700 --> 00:20:48.700
Notice a couple of pop guns.

191
00:20:48.700 --> 00:20:50.700
All right, this is turning into an all-star affair.

192
00:20:50.700 --> 00:20:52.700
Keith, you want another hand on the exchange?

193
00:20:52.700 --> 00:20:54.700
You sober?

194
00:20:54.700 --> 00:20:56.700
Will be by the time we get there.

195
00:20:56.700 --> 00:20:58.700
Got a bottle in the truck in case your hands get shaky.

196
00:20:58.700 --> 00:21:00.700
You know I could always count on you, Keith.

197
00:21:00.700 --> 00:21:02.700
All right, we'll gear you up as soon as we're done here.

198
00:21:02.700 --> 00:21:06.700
Matt, you can be the tip of the spear and we don't have to rob a guy from Delta.

199
00:21:06.700 --> 00:21:08.700
Now, be careful on the turnaround.

200
00:21:08.700 --> 00:21:11.700
If the Federal is a shooter, it's going to happen on the turnaround.

201
00:21:11.700 --> 00:21:13.700
Delta's Team 1 will be the lead vehicle.

202
00:21:13.700 --> 00:21:16.700
We can divide Team 2 between the carry car and the trail vehicle.

203
00:21:16.700 --> 00:21:18.700
Is that okay?

204
00:21:18.700 --> 00:21:23.700
Good. Now, Delta, if you can identify yourself so everyone knows who to hide behind if shit hits the fan.

205
00:21:23.700 --> 00:21:28.700
The most likely spot for a hit will be at the border crossing on the return.

206
00:21:28.700 --> 00:21:34.700
Anywhere along the way, anyone not in this room is a potential shooter.

207
00:21:34.700 --> 00:21:37.700
The op isn't over until we get back here.

208
00:21:37.700 --> 00:21:39.700
Okay?

209
00:21:39.700 --> 00:21:43.700
Be alert, be vigilant, and be aware. Let's go.

210
00:21:43.700 --> 00:21:44.700
You okay?

211
00:21:44.700 --> 00:21:53.420
What?

212
00:21:53.420 --> 00:21:56.420
Hey, I thought you were in prison.

213
00:21:56.420 --> 00:21:59.420
I needed somebody for this job.

214
00:21:59.420 --> 00:22:01.420
Good behavior or bad behavior?

215
00:22:01.420 --> 00:22:02.420
It's fine.

216
00:22:02.420 --> 00:22:12.260
Have you ever been over there?

217
00:22:12.260 --> 00:22:16.900
I worked in the waters.

218
00:22:16.900 --> 00:22:18.900
For the DEA?

219
00:22:18.900 --> 00:22:19.900
No.

220
00:22:19.900 --> 00:22:22.730
For who?

221
00:22:22.730 --> 00:22:31.420
For Mexico. I was a prosecutor.

222
00:22:31.420 --> 00:22:37.590
You're not American. What do you work for now?

223
00:22:37.590 --> 00:22:38.590
I go where I'm sent.

224
00:22:38.590 --> 00:22:42.190
Where were you sent from?

225
00:22:42.190 --> 00:22:44.600
Cartagena.

226
00:22:44.600 --> 00:22:57.680
I think it will make sense to your American ears.

227
00:22:57.680 --> 00:23:11.550
You will doubt everything that we do.

228
00:23:11.550 --> 00:23:13.550
Try this on. See if it fits.

229
00:23:13.550 --> 00:23:16.550
Is he CIA? Are you?

230
00:23:16.550 --> 00:23:18.550
He's a DOD advisor just like me.

231
00:23:18.550 --> 00:23:19.550
No, he's not.

232
00:23:19.550 --> 00:23:22.550
Let's just pay attention to Alejandro, and if he says do something, just do it.

233
00:23:22.550 --> 00:23:26.550
I'm not authorized to follow orders from Alejandro, especially in Mexico.

234
00:23:26.550 --> 00:23:28.550
Fine, then stay here.

235
00:23:28.550 --> 00:23:31.120
But you don't want to, do you?

236
00:23:31.120 --> 00:23:34.120
I just want to know what I'm getting into.

237
00:23:34.120 --> 00:23:40.120
Kate, you volunteered to get on this train because you know you're doing nothing in Phoenix.

238
00:23:40.120 --> 00:23:42.120
You're just sweeping up a fucking mess.

239
00:23:42.120 --> 00:23:46.120
In six months, every single house you raid will be rigged with explosives.

240
00:23:46.120 --> 00:23:49.120
Do you want to find the guys responsible, yes or no?

241
00:23:49.120 --> 00:23:50.120
Yes.

242
00:23:50.120 --> 00:23:51.120
Yes?

243
00:23:51.120 --> 00:23:54.010
Yes.

244
00:23:54.010 --> 00:23:56.010
This is where we start.

245
00:23:56.010 --> 00:23:57.010
Try it on.

246
00:23:57.010 --> 00:25:57.820
Went to visit President Diaz.

247
00:25:57.820 --> 00:26:00.820
Took 4,000 men with him.

248
00:26:00.820 --> 00:26:02.820
And it almost was called off.

249
00:26:02.820 --> 00:26:04.820
Some guy had a pistol.

250
00:26:04.820 --> 00:26:07.820
Gonna walk right up the taff and just blow his brains out.

251
00:26:07.820 --> 00:26:09.820
But it was avoided.

252
00:26:09.820 --> 00:26:11.820
4,000 troops.

253
00:26:11.820 --> 00:26:13.820
You think he felt safe?

254
00:26:13.820 --> 00:29:15.400
Body like that?

255
00:29:15.400 --> 00:29:19.000
People think they must have been involved.

256
00:29:19.000 --> 00:29:23.000
Those guys deserve such a death because they did something.

257
00:29:23.000 --> 00:29:26.000
It's brilliant what they do.

258
00:29:49.870 --> 00:34:37.440
Those aren't firecrackers.

259
00:34:37.440 --> 00:34:39.440
Red and Paula, two lanes left.

260
00:34:39.440 --> 00:35:16.600
Gun left.

261
00:35:16.600 --> 00:38:36.400
What are we doing?

262
00:38:36.400 --> 00:38:37.400
That was fucking illegal.

263
00:38:37.400 --> 00:38:39.400
You want to start a war?

264
00:38:39.400 --> 00:38:40.400
You're a fucking spook.

265
00:38:40.400 --> 00:38:41.400
And him?

266
00:38:41.400 --> 00:38:43.400
I mean, who the fuck is that?

267
00:38:43.400 --> 00:38:44.400
Told you you could stay here.

268
00:38:44.400 --> 00:38:46.400
Jesus Christ, Jesus Christ.

269
00:38:46.400 --> 00:38:47.400
You just spray bullets.

270
00:38:47.400 --> 00:38:49.400
Yeah, sure, there's just fucking civilians everywhere.

271
00:38:49.400 --> 00:38:50.400
I'm not a soldier.

272
00:38:50.400 --> 00:38:51.400
This is not what I do.

273
00:38:51.400 --> 00:38:53.400
Look, don't sell yourself short, all right?

274
00:38:53.400 --> 00:38:56.400
